Commit 99b3ce2ff805 added `Kill` / `NoteKill` / `KilledFor` so that emptying a holder parameter before shrinking a grow-only array satisfies §5.1. While `KilledFor` walks `TY_STRUCT` fields down to leaf slice/reference fields where `CanHoldViewInto(ft, arr)` holds, two checks in `NoteKill` prevent emptying a struct holding a `const u8[:]` slice:

1. Assigning a static slice directly to a slice field (`out.payload = ""`) returns early at `if (!target || !HoldsPlainRef(target) || IsRefOrSlice(target)) return;` because `target` is `TY_SLICE` (`IsRefOrSlice(target)` is `true` and `HoldsPlainRef(target)` is `false`). Similarly, `CheckRebind` (`out.ref .= null`) does not record a kill.
2. Assigning a whole struct value (`out = MessageView {}`) where a slice field defaults to `""` returns early at `if (!held.None() || held.unknown || !loc.Exact()) return;`. For a string literal `""`, `NoteLitElem` adds `{ root = nullptr, exact = true }` (static data) to `v.contents`, so `held.None()` (`alts.empty()`) is `false` even though static data borrows no array storage.

### Reproduction

```goose
struct MessageView {
    payload: const u8[:] = "",
}

fn parse_field<F>(buf: F&, out: MessageView&) -> bool {
    out.payload = "";
    buf.clear();
    buf.append("data");
    out.payload = buf[..];
    return true;
}

fn parse_whole<F>(buf: F&, out: MessageView&) -> bool {
    out = MessageView {};
    buf.clear();
    buf.append("data");
    out.payload = buf[..];
    return true;
}

fn main() {
    var buf: u8[>..] = [];
    var v = MessageView {};
    parse_field(buf, v);
    parse_whole(buf, v);
}
```

`goose --check` rejects both calls:

```text
test.goose:24: error: cannot call parse_field: it shrinks buf while out is still used, and out may refer into buf (§5.1)
    parse_field(buf, v);
```

If `payload` is changed to `payload: (u8&)? = null`, `out = MessageView {}` passes `goose --check` because `NoteLitElem` skips `v.isnull` and leaves `deep.roots` empty (`held.None() == true`), whereas `out.payload .= null` still fails because `CheckRebind` does not call `NoteKill`.

### Possible fix

- In `NoteKill`, treat a value whose roots are exclusively static data (`a.root == nullptr && a.exact`) as holding no runtime references, and allow leaf slice/reference fields on a `KillPath` (plus `v.isnull` in `CheckRebind`) to record a field kill when assigned static data or `null`.

