```

Expected `0.0 0.0`; with the definitions above both come back as `-0.0`. The sign carries into later math: `pow(abs(x), -1.0)` gives `-inf` instead of `inf`.

Found with a bit-level probe of 40 float operations against Rust (Goose v2026.3, gcc 15.2 and clang 21.1 at `-O2`). Still the same on `master` (eadca409f6).

A fix that clears the sign bit, for example binding to `fabs`/`fabsf` the way `stdlib/math.goose` binds `floor`, would match IEEE 754. 

