[`DeclStackLocal`](https://github.com/aardappel/goose/blob/9412b80f52d833c4697cffdbbf1f4eeb5195cd41/src/codegen_stmts.h#L791-L795) emits an uninitialized frame-object struct `T name;` and immediately calls `SaveBase` with `FoTailHdr(t, name).base`. [`GenFrameObjLit`](https://github.com/aardappel/goose/blob/9412b80f52d833c4697cffdbbf1f4eeb5195cd41/src/codegen_construct.h#L1329-L1363) then evaluates the fixed prefix fields (`header: read_header(fail)`) before writing `p_g.bytes_g.base = Top(stk)`.

When `read_header(true)` executes `return -1 from build`, [`EmitRestores`](https://github.com/aardappel/goose/blob/9412b80f52d833c4697cffdbbf1f4eeb5195cd41/src/codegen_frames.h#L1037-L1041) runs the registered restore `Top(stk) = p_g.bytes_g.base`, overwriting the data stack's `top` pointer with uninitialized C stack memory. The same path also applies when a frame object is a component of a `root struct` (`BindLocal` calls `DeclStackLocal` per component). Saving the stack's `Top(stk)` in a separate watermark local before prefix initialization (or initializing the tail header's `.base` before calling `SaveBase`) avoids reading an uninitialized field on early exit.

The [`return … from` contract](https://github.com/aardappel/goose/blob/9412b80f52d833c4697cffdbbf1f4eeb5195cd41/docs/goose_spec.md?plain=1#L3335-L3337) requires normal epilogues to restore all intermediate data-stack watermarks cleanly.

