-g (--debug-info) is --debug, plus C that LLDB, gdb and Visual Studio debug at the Goose level:

- a #line before every line of a function's C, so breakpoints, stepping and the call stack are in the .goose files;
- every C local declared at the function's top, so a Goose line is one breakpoint location, hit once (once a loop iteration);
- no inlining unless an -O is given, so every function keeps its frame;
- a resizable's count written as it changes, so it reads right from any frame;
- <stem>.debug.json beside the C: the Goose names, types and scopes of functions, locals, globals, struct fields and enum variants, for Goose support in a debugger.

